# Angular — Standards and Best Practices

## Technology Stack
- Angular 17+ (standalone components)
- TypeScript 5.x strict mode
- NgRx or Angular Signals for state management
- Angular Material or Tailwind CSS
- Jest + Angular Testing Library (90% coverage threshold)
- ESLint + Angular ESLint rules

## Architecture
```
core/       Singleton services, guards, interceptors (providedIn: 'root')
shared/     Reusable components, pipes, directives
features/   One folder per domain area (components + containers + services + models)
layout/     Shell, navigation, header components
```

## Key Rules
- `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component — no exceptions
- Standalone components preferred over NgModules (Angular 17+)
- Every production component must live in its own folder with four colocated
  files: `.component.ts`, `.component.html`, `.component.css`, and
  `.component.spec.ts` (never mix multiple components in the same directory)
- Use `templateUrl` and `styleUrls`; inline `template` / `styles` are forbidden
  outside test-only host components
- Group by role under `paginas/` (smart) and `componentes/` (presentational),
  then one subfolder per component
- Typed `FormGroup<T>` always — never untyped `FormGroup`
- All API calls go through feature services — never directly inside components
- Smart (container) components connect to state; dumb (presentational) components use `@Input`/`@Output` only
- **Signal-based `input()`/`output()`/`model()` are BLOCKED, not just discouraged**: confirmed
  2026-07-21 that Angular 17.3.12 + jest-preset-angular 13.1.6 in this repo throw `NG0950`/`NG0303`
  ("Input is required but no value is available yet" / "isn't a known property") for signal inputs
  under TestBed, on **both** `@Component()` and plain `@Directive()` — reproduced with a minimal
  isolated repro with cache cleared (`npx jest --clearCache`), not a fluke. Matches
  [angular/angular#54013](https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/54013). Keep using
  decorator-based `@Input()`/`@Output()` until the toolchain is upgraded and this is re-verified —
  do not let an enrichment/plan mandate Signal-based component APIs
- HTTP interceptor centralizes error mapping — services never catch HTTP errors individually
- JWT: functional `HttpInterceptorFn` with Bearer injection and single-flight refresh on 401 (`nucleo/auth`)
- Route auth: functional `CanActivateFn` guards (`guardAutenticacion`, `guardRoles`) + `*appSiTieneRol` — UX only; backend enforces `requerir_roles`

## Naming Conventions
| Element | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Components | PascalCase + suffix | `CandidateListComponent` |
| Services | PascalCase + suffix | `CandidateService` |
| Files | kebab-case | `candidate-list.component.ts` |
| Component folder | one folder per component | `componentes/tarjeta-resumen/` |

## Styling
- Global tokens and semantic classes live in `src/styles/design-tokens.css`
- `src/styles.css` is the global entry point; Tailwind theme lives in
  `tailwind.config.cjs`
- Component CSS contains only component-specific styles
- Reuse `--sst-*` tokens and `sst-*` classes before adding duplicated values
- Document new global tokens in `src/styles/README.md`

## Testing
- `TestBed` + Angular Testing Library
- `HttpClientTestingModule` for service HTTP tests
- 90% coverage enforced in `jest.config.ts`
- AAA pattern; test name: `should do something when condition`

## Git Workflow
- Branch naming: `feature/<ticket-id>-frontend`
- Commits: project's configured language, conventional commits
- **Never commit** `.angular/` cache, `node_modules/`, `dist/`, or `.env`
- ESLint `parserOptions.project` must point at `tsconfig.app.json` (not the empty root `tsconfig.json`)
- Avoid `!(observable | async)` in templates — use `as` + `else` instead
- On Windows: husky needs Git for Windows `sh` ahead of the WSL `bash.exe` stub, or commits fail with `HCS_E_SERVICE_NOT_AVAILABLE` (often misreported as ESLint failure). Prefer Git Bash or prepend `C:\Program Files\Git\bin` to `PATH` before `git commit` / `os-commit`
- CRLF/LF notices from git are informational when `core.autocrlf` is on — not failures
